<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Government of India</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1947">1947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Union Government of India</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> is the union government of the Republic of India, seated in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-delhi">New Delhi</a> and constituted since 1950 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-india">Constitution of India</a>. Its executive consists of the president and the council of ministers headed by the prime minister, responsible to Parliament; after independence in 1947 it integrated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> into the Indian Union.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/government-of-india.jpg" alt="Government of India" width="320" height="510" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Government of India · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_India.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Parliament concluded that a trading company could no longer govern India, and the <b>Government of India</b> Act of August 1858 transferred its territories, army and powers to the Crown.</blockquote><a href="/empire/british-raj">British Raj · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Chithira Thirunal died on 20 July 1991 after 67 years as ruler and titular Maharaja, and the <b>Government of India</b> issued a stamp on 6 November 1991 commemorating his reforms.</blockquote><a href="/empire/travancore">Travancore · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Under the covenants of merger these units passed to the union and were then taken over by the <b>Government of India</b>, which absorbed the State Forces into the Indian Army by 1951.</blockquote><a href="/empire/united-state-of-rajasthan">United State of Rajasthan · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>Under the <b>Government of India</b> Act of 1935, Aden was separated from India and became a Crown colony on 1 April 1937, as the Colony of Aden.</blockquote><a href="/state/aden-settlement">Aden Settlement</a></li><li><blockquote>Under the <b>Government of India</b> Act of 1935, the Aden Settlement was separated from British India and became a Crown colony on 1 April 1937, governed directly from London by a governor.</blockquote><a href="/state/colony-of-aden">Colony of Aden</a></li><li><blockquote>The <b>Government of India</b> Act of 1858 transferred power from the Company to the Crown, beginning the British Raj, and the Company was dissolved in 1874.</blockquote><a href="/state/company-rule-in-india">Company rule in India</a></li></ul></section>
